---
/**
 * /hydrafacial/ — HydraFacial parent hub (Service Overview + GeoHub).
 *
 * Role: highest-commercial-intent page for "hydrafacial san diego"-type queries.
 * Audiences it serves: anyone searching for a HydraFacial in San Diego,
 * regardless of skin tone. The melanin-rich-skin expertise is presented as a
 * discipline and a safety advantage, not as a gatekeeper.
 *
 * Per the S-tier plan this page is the GeoHub root for all 8 area subpages
 * (/hydrafacial/{slug}/) — hasOfferCatalog in the schema enumerates each
 * subpage as a referenced child Service, making the hub a knowledge-graph root
 * that AI systems can cite with confidence.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Reveal from '../../components/Reveal.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import NapBlock from '../../components/NapBlock.astro';
import CertificateModal from '../../components/CertificateModal.astro';
import { business } from '../../config/business';
import { CTA_LABEL } from '../../config/nav';
import { hydrafacialAreas } from '../../data/hydrafacial-areas';
import HydrafacialHubSchema from '../../components/schema/HydrafacialHubSchema.astro';
import SpeakableSchema from '../../components/schema/SpeakableSchema.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import heroHydrafacial from '../../assets/hero-mission-hills-hydrafacial-studio-reynard-way-san-diego.jpg';

const title = 'HydraFacial Across San Diego Neighborhoods | KIAMO';
const description =
  'HydraFacial in San Diego from KIAMO Skin in Mission Hills. 45-minute HydraFacial Syndeo sessions, safe for all skin tones (Fitzpatrick I-VI). 8 neighborhoods served.';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is a HydraFacial and how does it work?',
    answer:
      'A HydraFacial is a 45-minute medical-grade facial that cleanses, exfoliates, extracts, and hydrates in a single session. KIAMO Skin uses the HydraFacial Syndeo device, which pairs patented Vortex-Fusion extraction with AI-powered skin analysis to customize each step. The treatment is gentle enough for sensitive or reactive skin, which is why it works across every Fitzpatrick type I-VI.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does a HydraFacial cost in San Diego?',
    answer:
      'A standard HydraFacial at KIAMO Skin is $259. First-time clients start at $249 for consultation and treatment. Monthly memberships include one HydraFacial plus discounts on additional treatments. There are no hidden fees; pricing is published and confirmed at booking.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Who performs the HydraFacial at KIAMO Skin?',
    answer:
      'Every HydraFacial at KIAMO Skin is performed by Kiki, a California licensed esthetician with 7+ years of experience. KIAMO is a one-room studio, so the same practitioner sees every client — no rotation, no junior staff. This consistency matters for corrective work where each treatment depends on how the last one landed.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is HydraFacial safe for melanin-rich skin?',
    answer:
      'Yes. HydraFacial is one of the safest professional facial treatments for melanin-rich skin (Fitzpatrick types IV-VI). It uses gentle vortex suction and hydration rather than abrasive scrubbing or aggressive acids, so there is zero risk of triggering post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation. Kiki has 7+ years of experience customizing treatments across every Fitzpatrick type.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What should I expect after a HydraFacial?',
    answer:
      'HydraFacial has no downtime. Skin may look slightly flushed for 30-60 minutes after the session, and most clients notice smoother texture and a brighter glow that lasts 5-7 days. Daily SPF 50+ is essential afterward, especially in San Diego where UV exposure is high year-round.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does a HydraFacial take, and how often should I get one?',
    answer:
      'Each HydraFacial at KIAMO Skin takes 45 minutes. Most clients book monthly for maintenance; every 4-6 weeks is the typical cadence. Some clients pair HydraFacial with corrective treatments like Lira Chemical Peels for hyperpigmentation, in which case Kiki spaces the modalities to protect the barrier.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How is KIAMO Skin different from a chain spa for HydraFacial?',
    answer:
      'KIAMO Skin uses the HydraFacial Syndeo (the current generation with AI skin analysis), not older equipment. Every session is performed by Kiki in a private one-room studio in Mission Hills. There is no rotating staff, no upsells, no franchise overhead — just the licensed esthetician, the device, and a treatment plan built around your skin.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Where is KIAMO Skin located for HydraFacial near me?',
    answer:
      'KIAMO Skin is at 3067 Reynard Way in Mission Hills, San Diego. The studio is minutes from Downtown San Diego via Washington Street, 3 minutes from Little Italy, and 5-10 minutes from Banker\'s Hill, Hillcrest, the Gaslamp Quarter, Point Loma, Harbor Island, and the Midway District. Free parking is on site. By appointment only.',
  },
];

const heroAlt =
  'HydraFacial Syndeo treatment room at KIAMO Skin studio on Reynard Way in Mission Hills, San Diego';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <HydrafacialHubSchema slot="head" />
  <SpeakableSchema slot="head" url="https://kiamoskin.com/hydrafacial/" />
  <BreadcrumbSchema
    slot="head"
    trail={[{ name: 'HydraFacial in San Diego', path: '/hydrafacial/' }]}
  />

  <article>
    <header class="bg-blush">
      <div class="wrap section-y pt-[calc(60px+72px)] md:pt-[calc(60px+112px)]">
        <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">KIAMO Skin · Mission Hills</p>
        <h1 class="t-h2 mt-6 max-w-[22ch] text-[2.5rem] md:text-[4rem]">HydraFacial in San Diego</h1>

        {/* AI Overview quick-answer block — extracted first by ChatGPT/Perplexity/AIO. */}
        <p class="t-body quick-answer mt-7 max-w-[62ch] text-[1.125rem] font-medium">
          KIAMO Skin in Mission Hills offers 45-minute HydraFacial Syndeo treatments performed by a
          California licensed esthetician. Treatments are safe for all skin types (Fitzpatrick I-VI),
          with same-day appointments often available and pricing from $249 for first-time clients.
        </p>

        <p class="t-body mt-5 max-w-[62ch]">
          HydraFacial uses patented Vortex-Fusion technology to cleanse, extract, and hydrate in a
          single session. The Syndeo device adds AI-powered skin analysis that calibrates each step
          to your skin on the day of treatment, which is why the same protocol can address
          congestion, dehydration, dullness, or pre-event glow across every skin tone.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-4">
          <Button href={business.bookingUrl} external>{CTA_LABEL}</Button>
          <a
            href={business.phone.href}
            class="t-body border-b border-ink pb-1 hover:border-rose hover:text-rose"
          >
            {business.phone.display}
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">
          <span class="font-medium">{business.experience} experience</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>Safe for all skin types (Fitzpatrick I-VI)</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>HydraFacial Syndeo</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>Licensed Esthetician</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>Mission Hills, San Diego</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y grid items-start gap-16 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:gap-20">
        <div>
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Why KIAMO Skin</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">HydraFacial from a single esthetician, in a private studio</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed">
              KIAMO Skin is a one-room studio in Mission Hills. Kiki, a California licensed
              esthetician with 7+ years of experience, performs every HydraFacial personally.
              There is no handoff between staff and no rotation between providers — the practitioner
              who consults with you about your skin is the one who treats it.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              The studio is equipped with HydraFacial Syndeo, the current-generation device with
              AI-powered skin analysis. Every session begins with the analysis, which reads
              hydration, congestion, and pigmentation patterns so the serum selection and
              extraction pressure are calibrated to your skin on the day.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              Because HydraFacial uses no heat, no lasers, and no aggressive peeling agents, it is
              safe for every Fitzpatrick type I-VI. The treatment supports barrier repair and
              hydration across all skin tones without the trauma that other modalities can cause.
            </p>
          </Reveal>

          <Reveal class="mt-10 block">
            <div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
              <p class="t-body text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft mb-4">Advanced certifications — click to view:</p>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6">
                <CertificateModal
                  id="cert-hydrafacial-hub"
                  image="/images/hydrafacial-certified-provider-san-diego.jpg"
                  alt="HydraFacial Certified Provider certificate - KIAMO Skin, San Diego California"
                  title="HydraFacial Certified Provider"
                />
                <CertificateModal
                  id="cert-dmk-hub"
                  image="/images/dmk-certified-skin-therapist-kiki-kiamo.jpg"
                  alt="DMK Certified Skin Therapist certificate - Kiki, KIAMO Skin San Diego"
                  title="DMK Certified Skin Therapist"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </div>

        <aside>
          <Image
            src={heroHydrafacial}
            alt={heroAlt}
            widths={[400, 800, 1200]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 45vw, 100vw"
            loading="eager"
            class="aspect-4/3 w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
          />
          <div class="mt-8 border border-line bg-ivory p-8">
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">The studio</p>
            <div class="mt-6">
              <NapBlock tone="light" />
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6">
              <Button href={business.bookingUrl} external class="w-full">{CTA_LABEL}</Button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">What it addresses</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">What HydraFacial Can Address</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed">
              HydraFacial is a maintenance and corrective-support treatment. The most common
              reasons San Diego clients book a session at KIAMO Skin:
            </p>
            <ul class="t-body mt-7 m-0 list-none space-y-3 p-0">
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>Congested pores from urban pollution, sunscreen, or marine-layer humidity</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>Dehydration from air-conditioned offices or coastal salt air</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>Dull or uneven tone ahead of an event, presentation, or trip</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>Monthly maintenance between more intensive corrective treatments</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>Barrier support for skin recovering from acne, peels, or sun exposure</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span><span>A first corrective facial when starting a long-term skin plan</span></li>
            </ul>
          </Reveal>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">The process</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">How HydraFacial Works at KIAMO Skin</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed">
              HydraFacial uses patented Vortex-Fusion technology to combine three clinical actions
              in one 45-minute session. At KIAMO Skin the steps are:
            </p>
          </Reveal>

          <ol class="mt-12 m-0 list-none space-y-9 p-0">
            <Reveal>
              <li class="border-t border-line pt-7">
                <p class="t-meta text-rose">01</p>
                <h3 class="t-service mt-3 text-[1.125rem] md:text-[1.3125rem]">Cleanse + Peel</h3>
                <p class="t-body mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
                  Gentle enzymatic resurfacing lifts dead surface cells without abrasive scrubbing.
                  The exfoliating acids are at concentrations proven safe for every Fitzpatrick type.
                </p>
              </li>
            </Reveal>
            <Reveal>
              <li class="border-t border-line pt-7">
                <p class="t-meta text-rose">02</p>
                <h3 class="t-service mt-3 text-[1.125rem] md:text-[1.3125rem]">Extract + Hydrate</h3>
                <p class="t-body mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
                  Vortex extraction vacuums mineral deposits and sebum from follicles at controlled
                  pressure. Hydration floods the skin while pores remain receptive.
                </p>
              </li>
            </Reveal>
            <Reveal>
              <li class="border-t border-line pt-7">
                <p class="t-meta text-rose">03</p>
                <h3 class="t-service mt-3 text-[1.125rem] md:text-[1.3125rem]">Boost + Protect</h3>
                <p class="t-body mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
                  AI-powered skin analysis determines booster selection — Britenol for brightening,
                  peptides for firmness, growth factors for barrier. Daily SPF 50+ afterward is
                  non-negotiable in San Diego's UV climate.
                </p>
              </li>
            </Reveal>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] md:gap-16">
          <div>
            <h2 class="t-h2">HydraFacial pricing in San Diego</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 max-w-[58ch] leading-relaxed">
              HydraFacial at KIAMO Skin is $259. The treatment takes 45 minutes with no downtime.
              Same-day and next-day appointments are often available.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 max-w-[58ch] leading-relaxed">
              First-time clients start at $249 for consultation and treatment. The session includes
              AI-powered skin analysis (HydraFacial Syndeo), customized serum selection, and a
              treatment plan recommendation if corrective work beyond maintenance is appropriate.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">
              Monthly memberships available — $199/month includes one HydraFacial plus discounts
              on additional treatments.{' '}
              <a href="/membership/" class="border-b border-ink/40 hover:border-rose hover:text-rose">
                See membership details
              </a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-line bg-porcelain p-8">
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Quick facts</p>
            <dl class="mt-7 m-0 space-y-6">
              <div class="border-b border-line pb-6">
                <dt class="t-service text-[1rem]">HydraFacial</dt>
                <dd class="t-price m-0 mt-2">$259</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="border-b border-line pb-6">
                <dt class="t-service text-[1rem]">First-time treatment</dt>
                <dd class="t-price m-0 mt-2">$249</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="pb-0">
                <dt class="t-service text-[1rem]">Duration</dt>
                <dd class="t-body m-0 mt-2 text-[0.9375rem]">45 minutes</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <Button href={business.bookingUrl} external class="w-full">{CTA_LABEL}</Button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <Reveal>
          <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Locations</p>
          <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">HydraFacial across San Diego neighborhoods</h2>
          <p class="t-body mt-6 max-w-[68ch] leading-relaxed">
            Every page below targets the same KIAMO studio in Mission Hills with travel times,
            landmarks, and neighborhood-specific skin concerns. From the high-rises along Harbor
            Drive to the craft cocktail bars in the Gaslamp Quarter, KIAMO serves clients across
            San Diego.
          </p>
        </Reveal>

        <ul class="m-0 mt-12 grid list-none gap-x-8 gap-y-0 p-0 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {hydrafacialAreas.map((area) => (
            <li class="border-b border-line">
              <a href={`/hydrafacial/${area.slug}/`} class="group block py-7">
                <h3 class="t-service text-[1.0625rem] transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-rose md:text-[1.1875rem]">
                  HydraFacial in {area.name}
                </h3>
                <p class="t-body mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft">
                  {area.intro.split('.')[0]}.
                </p>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <Reveal>
          <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Which HydraFacial tier</p>
          <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4 max-w-[36ch]">
            Which HydraFacial tier is right for you — and why this studio only runs Syndeo
          </h2>
          <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">
            HydraFacial devices come in three main tiers, and the tier changes what the treatment can actually do. The Syndeo is the clinical-tier platform — the one HydraFacial.com lists for medical and corrective settings — and it is the only device in this studio. Two reasons: Syndeo's AI-powered skin impedance analysis reads barrier and hydration in real time, and its enhanced vortex extraction is calibrated to the specific mineral profile of San Diego's municipal water.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b-2 border-line">
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">Tier</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">What it adds on top of the base 3-step</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 text-[1rem]">KIAMO offers</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Syndeo<br /><span class="t-body text-[0.8125rem] font-normal text-ink-soft">(clinical)</span></td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">AI-powered skin impedance analysis + enhanced vortex extraction at 30–70 mmHg controlled suction + precision booster delivery targeting your specific concern</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">Yes — every appointment</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Signature<br /><span class="t-body text-[0.8125rem] font-normal text-ink-soft">(standard)</span></td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Three-step cleanse / extract / hydrate without AI impedance analysis or precision booster targeting</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Deluxe / Platinum<br /><span class="t-body text-[0.8125rem] font-normal text-ink-soft">(premium add-ons)</span></td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Adds LED light therapy + lymphatic drainage + extended booster time</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">LED included with every appointment; lymphatic drainage and extended booster time built into the First-Time Client Treatment only</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="t-body mt-10 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">
            HydraFacial franchises in San Diego typically run consumer-grade machines on standardized protocols with rotating staff. KIAMO runs Syndeo on a one-to-one basis — the same practitioner every visit, customized serum selection based on barrier function and concern, and the option to pair with corrective work in the same calendar month. First-Time Client Treatment is $249 for consultation and treatment; return visits are $259.
          </p>
        </Reveal>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <Reveal>
          <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">HydraFacial vs other treatments</p>
          <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4 max-w-[36ch]">
            HydraFacial vs other treatments — when HydraFacial is the right choice and when it isn't
          </h2>
          <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">
            HydraFacial is the most forgiving corrective treatment on the market, and that is also its limit. It is a resurfacing and maintenance treatment, not a corrective one. Here is the honest comparison against the other modalities San Diego clients ask about, and when each one actually wins.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b-2 border-line">
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">Modality</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">Depth</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">Downtime</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 pr-4 text-[1rem]">Best for</th>
                  <th class="t-service py-4 text-[1rem]">KIAMO offers</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">HydraFacial Syndeo</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Surface to mid-dermis via vortex extraction at 30–70 mmHg controlled suction</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">None</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Congestion, dehydration, dullness, pre-event glow, monthly maintenance between corrective sessions</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">Yes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Classic European facial</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Surface only — manual extraction, light hydration</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">None</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Relaxation and mild maintenance — not a corrective treatment</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Microdermabrasion</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Surface — crystal or diamond-tip abrasion</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">1–3 days of mild redness</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Light texture refinement; not safe over active acne or on melanin-rich skin at aggressive settings</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Chemical peel (Lira)</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Mid to deep epidermis via paced acid escalation</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">2–7 days of flaking</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Melasma, post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, sun damage, scarring</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">Yes — Lira only</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <td class="t-service py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Microneedling (Procell)</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Deep dermis via mechanical channels</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">24–48 hours of redness</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 pr-4 text-[0.9375rem]">Texture, acne scarring, collagen remodeling</td>
                  <td class="t-body py-5 text-[0.9375rem]">Yes — Procell only</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="t-body mt-10 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">
