            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">San Diego skin</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">Coastal, urban, and barrier-compromised skin in San Diego</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed">
              San Diego is one of the easier places in the country to damage a skin barrier, and
              one of the harder places to rebuild it. The same marine climate that makes the city
              pleasant also produces conditions that strip moisture from skin and clog pores faster
              than inland environments do.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              The marine layer rolls in from the Pacific between April and June and persists for
              much of the morning. High humidity and salt air leave a mineral residue on the skin
              that binds with sebum and clogs follicles. Downtown, the Gaslamp Quarter, and the
              Convention Center district add urban pollution — vehicle exhaust, construction dust,
              and recirculated office air conditioning that further dehydrates the barrier.
              Coastal neighborhoods from La Jolla to Pacific Beach, Ocean Beach, and Point Loma
              sit two miles or less from the Pacific and experience direct salt-spray exposure on
              most days.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              San Diego's municipal water supply is also among the hardest in California, with
              roughly 280-320 parts per million of dissolved calcium and magnesium. These minerals
              bond with sebum and skincare products, forming calcium carbonate deposits in
              follicles that ordinary cleansing cannot remove. Mission Hills residents and anyone
              who showers before bed experience this daily.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              HydraFacial Syndeo's Vortex-Fusion extraction was designed for exactly these
              conditions. The 30-70 mmHg controlled spiral suction pulls mineral deposits and
              sebum from follicles at calibrated pressure — strong enough to clear what at-home
              cleansing leaves behind, gentle enough to avoid the trauma that triggers
              post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation in all skin tones. The hydration step floods
              the skin with hyaluronic acid and antioxidants while pores remain receptive,
              rebuilding the barrier from the inside out rather than relying on topical products
              alone.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              For Downtown professionals, coastal residents, and anyone in Mission Hills or the
              surrounding neighborhoods, monthly HydraFacial maintenance is realistic when the
              studio is 5-10 minutes away. Each session is a reset for skin that has been working
              against salt air, hard water, and city pollution since the last visit.
            </p>
